# Deployed to ~/.config/xdg-terminals.list by setup-06-configs.sh.
#
# The default terminal, in the format of the XDG terminal spec: desktop entry
# IDs, one per line, highest priority first. Ubuntu 26.04 routes Ctrl+Alt+T
# through xdg-terminal-exec (the "exec" of the deprecated
# org.gnome.desktop.default-applications.terminal key), and this is where
# xdg-terminal-exec looks first - the user file wins over Ubuntu's own list in
# /usr/share/xdg-terminal-exec/, which puts Ptyxis first. "Open in Terminal"
# and every other launch through xdg-terminal-exec follow it too.
#
# The entry comes from setup-03-alacritty.sh; until that has run, the line
# matches nothing and xdg-terminal-exec falls through to Ubuntu's list.
Alacritty.desktop
